From: Mark Harfouche <mark@ramonaoptics.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Depend on segment-anything-py, the real PyPI distribution

The `segment_anything` name upstream declares is not a distribution that
exists on PyPI: the package that provides the `segment_anything` module is
published as `segment-anything-py`, and that is what the conda-forge
`segment-anything` package installs. As declared, the requirement can never
be satisfied and `pip check` always reports it as missing.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 85d03a1..fee64be 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -14,7 +14,7 @@ install_deps = [
     'imagecodecs',
     'roifile',
     'fill-voids',
-    'segment_anything',
+    'segment-anything-py',
 ]
 
 image_deps = ['nd2', 'pynrrd']
